## Risks

- **Rule 7.** The history decides nothing. Undo and Redo only send old field values through `updateDeck`, and the server still enforces D1–D5 and the caps. A redo can put back a card a deck being compared now holds (comparing is not an edit), and it shows as any existing clash does (R251). Refusing that redo was rejected as a client-side rule.
- **One-screen layout (R1581000, e2e spec 46).** Two more 44 px buttons in the header row can push the save status to a second row on a 390 px phone. The page stays one screen because `ws-layout` is the scrolling region. Do not shrink type.
- **Stale closures.** `editDeck` reads the deck from `store.getSnapshot()`, not from the render, so two edits in one tick still record the right `before`. The key listener goes through the ref, as in ReplayPlayer.
- **i18n.** `i18n.test.ts` fails on any new `t()` literal without a zh-CN entry. Add only "Undo" and "Redo".
- **Hooks order.** The new `useState`/`useRef`/`useEffect` calls must run on every render. There is no early return in `DeckWorkshop`, so keep it that way.

